this is a version of vtparse that also creates a python module, vtparse.py,
when you execute make(1).

the vtparse_table.[ch] are run through "gcc -E -" for preprocessing, and
this output is fed to vtparse_gen.py to produce vtparse.py.

the vtparse.py module contains 2 public items:

    - clean(text-to-clean) strips terminal control codes from text-to-clean
      and returns the cleaned text

    - p = VTParser(callback)
      p(text-to-parse)

      the callback fcn callback() is called as

        callback(action, ch)
      
      where "action" is one of the VTPARSE_ACTION_xxx constants, and ch is
      either 0 or the character just read. see the src for details.

DO NOT run unicode through this -- you will not be happy.

this has been tested with python-2.7.18, 3.14.3, 3.11.2, and 3.6.12.

